<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Long Turkish War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1593–1606</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Thirteen Years' War (1593–1606), Fifteen Years' War · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-habsburg-wars">Ottoman–Habsburg wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Long Turkish War was fought from 1593 to 1606 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, Wallachia and Moldavia joining the Habsburg side for a time. Neither side won decisively, despite the Ottoman victory at Mezőkeresztes in 1596. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-zsitvatorok">Peace of Zsitvatorok</a> of 1606 treated the Habsburg emperor as an equal of the sultan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/long-turkish-war.jpg" alt="Long Turkish War" width="320" height="271" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Folk art painting · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Turkish_war_1683.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
